  "note": "Municipal elections, May 1958. There was no contest after withdrawals: the ten rival Nationalist candidates for the seven West Ward seats settled, and three withdrew, leaving the new council 14 Unionists and seven Nationalists (Irish News, 8 May 1958, p. 6; Irish News, 9 May 1958, p. 1). Seven Unionist nominations for seven seats, returned unopposed. Returned unopposed."
